    "q-161253": {
      "dom_id": "step-q161253",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "Consider the vector field $F$ and the surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v),$ where\n\n$$\nF(x,y,z)=⟨z,\\,xz,\\,yz⟩,\\,r(u,v)=⟨u,\\,{u}^{2},\\,v⟩,\\,(u,v)\\in D⊂{R}^{2}.\n$$\n\nIf the flux of $F$ across $S$ with respect to $n$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{D}auv+b{u}^{2}v\\,\\text{d}A\n$$\n\nwhat is the value of $a+b?$",
      "worked_solution": "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $F$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{S}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWe first compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}({u}^{2}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,2u,\\,0⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}({u}^{2}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,0,\\,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 2u & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}2u & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|,\\,-|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|,\\,|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2u \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2u,\\,-1,\\,0⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $r(u,v)$ into $F(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v)) & =⟨z,\\,xz,\\,yz⟩{|}_{x=u\\,y={u}^{2}\\,z=v} \\\\  & =⟨v,\\,uv,\\,{u}^{2}v⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the dot product of $F$ and ${r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}) & =⟨v,\\,uv,\\,{u}^{2}v⟩\\cdot ⟨2u,\\,-1,\\,0⟩ \\\\  & =v\\cdot 2u+uv\\cdot (-1)+{u}^{2}v\\cdot 0 \\\\  & =2uv-uv+0 \\\\  & =uv.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}1\\cdot uv+0\\cdot {u}^{2}v\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, \n\n$$\na+b=1+0=1.\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
